==English==
{{ety|en|:af|head|start}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-au-head start.ogg|a=AU}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} An [[advantage]] consisting in starting a [[competition]] or [[task]] earlier than might be expected; given (or taken), for example, prior to the beginning of a race.
#: {{ux|en|Fred gave his younger brother a five-minute '''head start''' in the Easter egg hunt.}}
#: {{ux|en|I want to set off at dawn to get a '''head start''' over the competition.}}
#: {{ux|en|a day and a half '''head start'''}}
# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} A [[factor]] conducive to [[superiority]] and [[success]].
#: {{ux|en|His father's money gave him a '''head start''' in life.}}

